<group prefix="WebGpuSharp.FFI.">
    <comment location="BufferHandle">
        <summary>
            The Buffer represents a block of memory that can be used to store raw data to use
            in GPU operations.
        </summary>
    </comment>
    <group prefix="BufferHandle.">
        <comment location="GetMapState">
            <summary>An enumerated value representing the mapped state of the Buffer.</summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="GetSize">
            <summary>Returns the size of the buffer in bytes.</summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="GetUsage">
            <summary>Returns the allowed usages of the Buffer</summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="MapAsync">
            <param name="callbackInfo">Callback to be called when the buffer is mapped.</param>
            <returns>The future for the callback.</returns>
        </comment>
        <comment location="SetLabel">
            <summary>Sets a label on the Buffer.</summary>
            <param name="label">The label to set.</param>
        </comment>
        <comment location="GetConstMappedRange">
            <summary>                
                Returns a const pointer to beginning of the mapped range.
                It must not be written; writing to this range causes undefined behavior.
                See MappedRangeBehavior for error conditions and guarantees.
                This function is safe to call inside spontaneous callbacks (see CallbackReentrancy).
            </summary>
            <param name="offset">Byte offset relative to the beginning of the buffer.</param>
            <param name="size">                
                Byte size of the range to get.
                If this is
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.WebGPU_FFI.WHOLE_MAP_SIZE"/>
                , it defaults to `buffer.size - offset`.
                The returned pointer is valid for exactly this many bytes.
            </param>
        </comment>
        <comment location="ReadMappedRange">
            <summary>                
                Copies a range of data from the buffer mapping into the provided destination pointer.
                See MappedRangeBehavior for error conditions and guarantees.
                This function is safe to call inside spontaneous callbacks (see CallbackReentrancy).
                
                In Wasm, this is more efficient than copying from a mapped range into a `malloc`'d range.
            </summary>
            <param name="offset">Byte offset relative to the beginning of the buffer.</param>
            <param name="data">Destination, to read buffer data into.</param>
            <param name="size">Number of bytes of data to read from the buffer. (Note <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.WebGPU_FFI.WHOLE_MAP_SIZE"/> is *not* accepted here.)</param>
            <returns><see cref="WebGpuSharp.Status.Error"/> if the copy did not occur.</returns>
            </comment>
            <comment location="WriteMappedRange">
                <summary>                    
                    Copies a range of data from the provided source pointer into the buffer mapping.
                    See MappedRangeBehavior for error conditions and guarantees.
                    This function is safe to call inside spontaneous callbacks (see CallbackReentrancy).
                    In Wasm, this is more efficient than copying from a `malloc`'d range into a mapped range.
                </summary>
                <param name="offset">Byte offset relative to the beginning of the buffer.</param>
                <param name="data">Source, to write buffer data from.</param>
                <param name="size">Number of bytes of data to write to the buffer. (Note <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.WebGPU_FFI.WHOLE_MAP_SIZE"/> is *not* accepted here.)</param>
				<returns><see cref="WebGpuSharp.Status.Error"/> if the copy did not occur.</returns>
			</comment>
        </group>
    </group>